-- title:
--   Queried Paley prefix population bounds
-- statement:
--   Let $F=\mathbb{F}_{2659}$ with quadratic character $\chi$. For a finite set $H\subseteq F$, write $p_H(x)=|\{a\in H:\chi(x-a)=1\}|$. This bundle stores the literal list of queried triples $(h,k,B)$, where $h$ is the high-set cardinality, $k$ is the permitted number of failures, and $B$ is the chosen population limit. The intended inequality for each listed triple is
--
--   $$|H|=h\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\bigl|\{x\in F\setminus H:p_H(x)\ge\max(h-k,0)\}\bigr|\le B.$$
--
--   The list supplies the numerical population limits used by the unary rank recipe. The associated coefficient certificates and their bound lemmas establish these inequalities uniformly over all eligible sets.
-- source:
--   Formalization for https://prove2.me/campaigns/block-sensitivity-vs-sensitivity; task source research/hec-lean433/RiemannHypothesisCurves/PaleyUnary/Data.lean lines 15–217; SHA256 cbef574f04f20f10d1e3f24cc13bdf8bead7e437b07a581cfd919403a448b0a8; original campaign checkpoint SHA256 ed463039fb45e15e0e62a99e149dc811ac44ae8f790a5ae03ea5a7501f0639df.

